:: T: VehVeh doAtMarket [topic] {"position":"6525,1175","size":"100,100"}
{=

(storylet: when
(passage:) contains "NPC"
and $char's VehVeh's opinion's 2nd >= 10
and $char's VehVeh's location is "The Grand Exchange"
and $char's player's timerCooldown does not contain "T: VehVeh doAtMarket"
)

(urgency: 1)
(metadata:
"NPC", "VehVeh",
"title", "Chatting About the Grand Exchange",
"topic", "This place is huge, and crowded, too...",
"topicDetail", "Small talk about the market is only second to small talk about the weather.",
"cooldown", 1,
"talked", (a:),
"addCode", [],
)

$cssColumnParent[

$cssColumnChild[
	$cssBox[
    	($funcImage: (passage: "S: VehVeh atMarket")'s img)
         $cssBoxItem[''(print: (passage:)'s title )''<br>(print: (passage:)'s topicDetail)]
    ]
]

$cssColumnChild[

<!--VehVehLine short hand-->
(set: _line to (hook: "VehVehLine"))

$cssDesc[''You: //(print: (passage:)'s topic)//'']
<br>

_line["Yeah, it //is// a Grand Exchange, after all,"] Veh-Veh gazes up at the red steel dome above, which has replaced most of the sky, and ceiling murals - depicting the reigns and deeds of various emperors - function like guiding stars for the lost customer. _line["Is there one where you're from?"]
<br>
($funcInnerConvo: (dm:
    "<!--A-->\"Yes, but the Grand Exchange in Kom City isn't as large as this one.\"", "inKom",
    "<!--B-->\"Bakho dahak isn't known for our commerce, but yes, we do have a few.\"", "fewBakho",
    "<!--C-->\"In the heartlands, there are domes as far as the eyes can see.\"", "heartlandDomes",
))
<br>


<!--inKom-->
[
Kom City is far from the largest settlement in Bakho dahak, and its relatively humble Exchange branch reflects this. In actuality, the so-called "city" is only an outcrop of the much larger Bakho University - your alma mater.
<br>
_line["Oh? Glad to know Apesai isn't the least in the land at //something//,"] Veh-Veh grins as if she has won some unspoken competition. _line["If Apesai is known for anything, it would be its Grand Exchange. Although, I hope we'll have more to offer in the future."]
<br>
She means her school.
<br>
($funcInnerConvo: (dm:
    "<!--A-->\"Anyhow, what's there to do here?\"", "whatsThere",
))
<br>
](inKom|


<!--fewBakho-->
[
There are around five Grand Exchanges in Bakho, to be exact, with a one more under construction, which is quite few for such a large province. But, things are changing fast under the Reclamation. Too fast. Many are finding themselves falling through the cracks, you included.
<br>
_line["Well, the whole of Askava only has this one,"] Veh-Veh gestures at the dome above. _line["If there can only ever be one, it should at least be this big. We are at the terminus of the Exchange network, after all."]
<br>
You cannot tell if she is proud or weary of that fact.
<br>
($funcInnerConvo: (dm:
    "<!--A-->\"Anyhow, what's there to do here?\"", "whatsThere",
))
<br>
](fewBakho|


<!--heartlandDomes-->
[
It is true that in the heartlands, one can find always find red steel domes, crystal-encrusted domes, even tacky gilded domes wherever one goes. And there are towers too - ivory minarets, bare metal spires, glass skyscrapers, and so on. But all of this is trivially true, like saying a forest is full of trees. The wealth of many civilizations pour into the heartlands and their numerous Grand Exchanges. You are just showing off.
<br>
_line["So I've read,"] Veh-Veh nods, eyes dimmed as though seeing the magnificent scene in her own mind. _line["Silly of me to have asked."]
<br>
($funcInnerConvo: (dm:
    "<!--A-->\"Anyhow, what's there to do here?\"", "whatsThere",
))
<br>
](heartlandDomes|


<!--whatsThere-->
[
_line["Buying and selling things, what else? It's the //market district//,"] she chuckles, then clears her throat. _line["I'm joking. Of course you know that.
<br>
"Nearly everything that can be found in Askava is sold here. I'm to fetch supplies for the school; there's a whole floor that only sells magical ingredients, same goes with books. It's heavenly, but the price is //extra// steep, so you should really have your rials ready."]
<!--"spindle" convo, mode 1 (exit available at the start)-->
<!--better idea to use the standard variable $stuff's convoChoices so that it can be reused at will in the content temp vars (I've removed automated spindle convo since conversations can go on a bit longer)-->
(set: $stuff's convoChoices to (dm:
     "<!--B-->\"Why are things so expensive here?\"", "spindleWhyExpensive",
     "<!--A-->\"Truly? I can buy //everything// here?\"", "spindleEverything",
     "<!--C-->\"Can one make a decent profit selling things in the Exchange?\"", "spindleSellProfit",
     "<!--D-->\"What else is there to spend my money on, other than ingredients and books?\"", "spindleElse",
     "<!--E-->\"I see. That's all I wanted to know.\"", "exitLink",
))

($funcSpindleConvo: $stuff's convoChoices, 1)
](whatsThere|


(set: _spindleWhyExpensive to [{
Veh-Veh sighs, _line["I wonder the same thing.
<br>
"It probably has something to do with the fact that Apesai produces very few things of its own. We are on a rocky island, as you may have noticed. There is precious little land for crops or large workshops.
<br>
"Most of what we need is imported. For instance, mainland Askava supplies the majority of our food and fresh water. And, the various guilds charge heavily for their trouble."]
<br>
($funcInnerConvo: $stuff's convoChoices)
<br>
}])<!--end of _spindleWhyExpensive-->


(set: _spindleEverything to [{
Veh-Veh suppresses a chuckle, _line["Heh, no, I'm being hyperbolic.
<br>
"The most valuable goods here are bulk exports, like compacted vehzin, for example. Unless you're a registered exporter, us regular folks are left with whatever that's come loose or won't fit on their cargo.
<br>
"And it goes without saying, but 'everything' means 'everything //legal//'. But, Askava is also known for... well, never mind."]
<br>
Any number of thing can fit into that gap: the mind-bending farabek, the artifacts of Navveh and the Askavan Queendoms, Keshan literature, and so on. These are the things you were warned about before leaving the heartlands.
<br>
($funcInnerConvo: $stuff's convoChoices)
<br>
}])<!--end of _spindleEverything-->


(set: _spindleSellProfit to [{
Veh-Veh gives you a confused look, _line["No, not unless you're part of some merchant's guild, and if you //are//, then you would already have known that.
<br>
"Some shops will accept resale from non-members, but you should treat it like a small step up from tossing your belongings into the sea. The guilds are smarter than to let us compete with their merchants and workshops.
<br>
"I'd bet that if it wasn't for the guilds, a third of those pilgrims would stay here in Apesai instead of continuing into the inland desert. Not all of them believe in prophecy."]

<br>
($funcInnerConvo: $stuff's convoChoices)
<br>
}])<!--end of _spindleSellProfit-->


(set: _spindleElse to [{
Veh-Veh thinks about it for a moment, _line["If you plan to travel, you'll want to visit the dry goods warehouse. Our teachers' rule of thumb is to buy according to their expected travel days, plus half.
<br>
"Also, it's always a good idea to have some spare vehzin ready - that's obvious for us magi. But, if I were you, I'll wait to buy inland. I heard there's a shortage; something's going on in the mines.
<br>
"And, you can always buy rial itself, if you happen to have foreign currencies. Those things are dead weight in the Exchange, though I like to keep a little bit as souvenir, even keshi, though don't tell anyone that..."]
<br>
($funcInnerConvo: $stuff's convoChoices)
<br>
}])<!--end of _spindleElse-->


(set: _exitLink to [{
_line["Right, right,"] she nods. _line["Truth be told, I only shop here because I have to. But if you're not in a hurry, I'll advise that you save your rial and buy things inland. The merchants here don't really need to get any richer than they already are."]
<br>
($funcInnerConvo: (dm:
    "<!--A-->\"Understood.\"", "doneChoices",
))
<br>
}])<!--end of _exitLink-->


<!--doneChoices-->
[
<!--busy or not?-->
(set: _busy to true)
(if: $char's VehVeh's energy's 1st > 0)[(set: _busy to false)]

(if: _busy)[
_line["Anyways,"] she sighs, restlessly shuffling. _line["I still have some more chores to do. We'll catch up again soon, if you're still in Apesai."]
]

(else:)[
_line["Anyways,"] she says. _line["We can keep talking, if you don't mind following me on my chores."]
]

<br>
---
<ol>
($funcNPCTopics: "You have kept her for long enough. She needs to get on with things.", "Be seeing you, Veh-Veh. Goodbye.")
</ol>
](doneChoices|

]<!--end child-->
]<!--end parent-->